## DESCRIPTION
##   Find a Normal Vector
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject(Geometry)
## DBchapter(Vector geometry)
## DBsection(Cross product)
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Union College)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## AuthorText1('Rogawski')
## EditionText1('1')
## Section1('12.5')
## Problem1('11 15')
## KEYWORDS('Vector', 'Normal', 'Perpendicular')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserVectorUtils.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Vector");

#  The points A, B and C
$A = non_zero_point3D();
$B = non_zero_point3D();
$C = non_zero_point3D();

#  Vectors in the plane
$AB = Vector($B - $A);
$AC = Vector($C - $A);

#  The normal vector
$N = $AB x $AC;

#  Fix it up if AB is parallel to AC
if (abs($N) == 0) {
    ($a, $b, $c) = $AB->value;
    if ($a == 0 && $b == 0) {
        $C = $C + Vector(-$c, 0, $a);
    } else {
        $C = $C + Vector(-$b, $a, 0);
    }
    $AC = Vector($C - $A);
    $N  = $AB x $AC;
}

BEGIN_PGML

Find a vector [`\vec{v}`] that is perpendicular to the plane through the
points

[```A = [$A],\qquad B = [$B],\quad{\text{and}}\quad C = [$C]```]

[`\vec{v}= \;`] [_]{$N->cmp(parallel=>1)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
If the vector is perpendicular to _two_, vectors in the plane, it will be
perpendicular to them all.  Can you find two vectors in this plane?
END_PGML_HINT
ENDDOCUMENT();
